$CATEGORY: Q13 - Arrays and strings

::Q1301::
array - a collection of values in which all the values might have different types. {FALSE}

::Q1302::
element - One of the values in an array. The [] operator selects elements. {TRUE}

::Q1303::
index - an integer variable or value used to indicate an element of an array. {TRUE}

::Q1304::
allocate - to reserve memory for an array or other object. In Java, the new operator allocates memory. {TRUE}

::Q1305::
reference - a value that indicates a storage location. In a memory diagram, a reference appears as an arrow. {TRUE}

::Q1306::
alias - a variable that refers to the same object as another variable. {TRUE}

::Q1307::
traversal - looping through the elements of an array (or other collection). {TRUE}

::Q1308::
reduce {
    ~ a traversal pattern used to find a particular element of an array
    = a traversal pattern that combines the elements of an array into a single value
}

::Q1309::
search {
    = a traversal pattern used to find a particular element of an array
    ~ a traversal pattern that combines the elements of an array into a single value
}

::Q1310::
accumulator - a variable used to accumulate results during a traversal. {TRUE}

::Q1311::
histogram {
    =an array of integers in which each integer counts the number of values that fall into a certain range.
    ~an alternative syntax for traversing the elements of an array (or other collection)
} 

::Q1313::
enhanced for loop {
    ~an array of integers in which each integer counts the number of values that fall into a certain range.
    =an alternative syntax for traversing the elements of an array (or other collection)
} 